KZ2 patch 6080: resident raw vertex streams wired into the live draw (LD_VTX_RES; design F step 1,
sub-step b2). Patch 6079 added the pure part (rsx_vtx_res.h); this patch uses it. Default off.

LD_VTX_RES=1 (or verify) with LD_VTX_GPU=1 (patch 2076) and the write watch (patch 6077, on by default): a draw that
2076 would fetch on the GPU maps each merged raw span's 4 KB pages into a resident pool instead of copying the spans
into the upload ring every draw; the ring gets only the table (48-byte rows) and the per-span block lists.
1. rsx_vp_decompiler.c/.h: rsx_vp_vgpu_resident (set once by the live draw) makes 2076's variant declare t22 (the pool)
   and read through the block lists (RSX_VR_HLSL_HEAD, RSX_VR_SHARED, RSX_VR_HLSL_TAIL).
2. rsx_live_draw.c: ld_vr_mode() (decided once, at the first of the buffer setup and the root signature: a third
   vertex-stage root SRV, t22); the pool is an
   upload-heap buffer of LD_VTX_RES_MB (default 128) MB, mapped for good; if it fails, GPU fetch goes off (CPU fetch).
   The PSO key of a resident GPU-fetch pipeline carries a tag, so a stored 2076 pipeline is never taken for it.
   ld_vr_map_draw() after rsx_vg_plan: vr_map_span per span (frame = fence_value + 1, held while the draw is mapped;
   completed = the fence's completed value, capped at fence_value); at the t22 bind the draw's blocks are stamped
   again with fence_value + 1 of that moment, the signal of the list it is recorded in (vr_stamp, an earlier change: the
   vertex ring, VS-constant ring, descriptor ring and texture uploads can each flush between the map and the record); a
   failed map keeps the draw on the CPU path (counted as [vtx-gpu] unmapped). The block write becomes vr_write_table.
   [vtx-res] every 60 flips: draws, failed maps, pages, copies, stands, clean reuses, collects, retires, evictions,
   alloc failures, bad (verify).
3. Epochs (rsx_live_draw_vr_epoch, rsx_live_draw.h): each drain pass (a new put), each JUMP and CALL (an SPU-patched
   hole or a new segment), each NV406E semaphore ACQUIRE (it orders the RSX after a producer's writes but
   ends no pass when the label is already there, and KZ2 runs with GCM_SEMA_ACQUIRE unset; an earlier change: an acquire whose
   label does not hold the value yet holds the stands until it does, rsx_live_draw_vr_acquire with vr_acquire and
   vr_hold_check at each draw, as the producer can still write after it; the [vtx-res] line counts holds, releases,
   held maps, overflows and pending), rsx_live_draw_before_guest_sync, rsx_live_draw_writeback_range, rsx_live_draw_blit and
   rsx_live_draw_resolve_blit. ASSUMPTION (6079's guest-sync rule): no guest write lands on a page a later draw of the
   same epoch reads; LD_VTX_RES=verify checks every reuse against the checksum of its copy, and splits a mismatch by
   the rule that kept the page (stand / clean) and by whether the draw's own bytes changed (read / unread).
Own design; not from upstream. Host test of the pure part: tools/runtime/test_vtx_res.sh (6079).

