+ * reads through the lists (RSX_VR_SHARED). Frames are fence values: the map stamps a draw's blocks with fence_value + 1
+ * (held while the draw is mapped, as completed <= fence_value), and the record stamps them again with the signal of
+ * the list the draw is recorded in (vr_stamp at the t22 bind, after every flush the draw can cause: vertex ring,
+ * VS-constant ring, descriptor ring, texture uploads; an earlier change); a block is reused only when the GPU has completed
+ * that value. Epochs end wherever the walker can see newer guest bytes: each drain pass, each JUMP and CALL, each NV406E
+ * acquire (cellGcmSys.c), each write of RSX output to guest memory (rsx_live_draw_before_guest_sync, writeback_range,
